{
    "_comment": [
        "SAT-SA capability registry: the eight SOC capabilities named in the SIH",
        "problem statement.",
        "",
        "This file answers 'what SOC capability can SAT-SA actually assess from the",
        "evidence this CSE submitted?' It is NOT a risk model and produces no",
        "capability scores.",
        "",
        "EVIDENCE REFERENCES",
        "Every evidence item is a canonical_path that already exists in",
        "framework/canonical/canonical_schema.json. When a concept is named it is an",
        "existing concept from framework/config/mappings.json. CapabilityRegistry",
        "rejects the registry at load time if any path or concept is unknown, so no",
        "definition can invent a canonical field.",
        "",
        "An evidence item whose canonical field has NO concept in mappings.json is",
        "declared but undiscoverable: it can never be satisfied from a source column",
        "today. It is still listed, because the capability requirement is real and the",
        "gap is the honest answer. Such items appear in evidence_missing and are",
        "flagged concept=null.",
        "",
        "MINIMUM EVIDENCE",
        "minimum_evidence.primary : how many PRIMARY items must be satisfied for",
        "                              AVAILABLE.",
        "minimum_evidence.total   : how many items (primary + supporting) must be",
        "                              satisfied for AVAILABLE.",
        "These are explicit and configurable. Statuses are computed from them; no",
        "status is hardcoded per dataset.",
        "",
        "INDICATOR CATEGORIES",
        "Names come from the existing framework.features.feature_registry",
        "FEATURE_REGISTRY, and indicator_emitted_by records which existing detector",
        "currently emits each one. 'declared' means the relationship is registered but",
        "no detector produces it yet. This layer never generates findings."
    ],


    "capabilities": {

        "THREAT_DETECTION": {

            "name": "Threat Detection",
            "description":
                "Evidence that the CSE detects and classifies threats, including severity and threat categorisation of incoming alert activity.",
            "primary_evidence": [
                {
                    "canonical_path": "alert_context.severity",
                    "concept": "SECURITY_SEVERITY",
                    "role": "severity of detected alerts"
                },
                {
                    "canonical_path": "alert_context.category",
                    "concept": "THREAT_CATEGORY",
                    "role": "threat categorisation of detected alerts"
                },
                {
                    "canonical_path": "classification_context.security_label",
                    "concept": "SECURITY_LABEL",
                    "role": "security classification applied to detections"
                }
            ],
            "supporting_evidence": [
                {
                    "canonical_path": "alert_context.timestamp",
                    "concept": "EVENT_TIMESTAMP",
                    "role": "when detection occurred, required for detection cadence"
                },
                {
                    "canonical_path": "alert_context.alert_id",
                    "concept": null,
                    "role": "alert identity, required to distinguish detections from other records"
                }
            ],
            "minimum_evidence": {"primary": 2, "total": 3},
            "indicator_categories": ["SEVERITY_RISK"],
            "indicator_emitted_by": {
                "SEVERITY_RISK": "declared"
            }

        },


        "INVESTIGATION": {

            "name": "Investigation",
            "description":
                "Evidence that the CSE investigates detections, including recorded analysis and its outcome.",
            "primary_evidence": [
                {
                    "canonical_path": "investigation_context.notes",
                    "concept": "INVESTIGATION_EVIDENCE",
                    "role": "recorded investigation analysis"
                }
            ],
            "supporting_evidence": [
                {
                    "canonical_path": "investigation_context.root_cause_identified",
                    "concept": null,
                    "role": "whether investigation reached a root cause"
                },
                {
                    "canonical_path": "investigation_context.evidence_available",
                    "concept": null,
                    "role": "whether investigative evidence was retained"
                },
                {
                    "canonical_path": "investigation_context.remediation_identified",
                    "concept": null,
                    "role": "whether investigation identified remediation"
                },
                {
                    "canonical_path": "entity_context.entity_name",
                    "concept": "USER_IDENTIFIER",
                    "role": "identity of the analyst or owner performing the investigation"
                },
                {
                    "canonical_path": "alert_context.timestamp",
                    "concept": "EVENT_TIMESTAMP",
                    "role": "investigation reference time"
                }
            ],
            "minimum_evidence": {"primary": 1, "total": 2},
            "indicator_categories": ["INVESTIGATION_QUALITY"],
            "indicator_emitted_by": {
                "INVESTIGATION_QUALITY": "framework.supervision.execution_gap_engine.ExecutionGapEngine"
            }

        },


        "ESCALATION": {

            "name": "Escalation",
            "description":
                "Evidence that the CSE escalates detections when severity or handling thresholds require it.",
            "primary_evidence": [
                {
                    "canonical_path": "response_context.escalation_status",
                    "concept": "ESCALATION_STATUS",
                    "role": "recorded escalation state of a case"
                }
            ],
            "supporting_evidence": [
                {
                    "canonical_path": "alert_context.severity",
                    "concept": "SECURITY_SEVERITY",
                    "role": "severity that drives escalation decisions"
                },
                {
                    "canonical_path": "response_context.acknowledgement_time",
                    "concept": null,
                    "role": "acknowledgement timing relative to escalation"
                }
            ],
            "minimum_evidence": {"primary": 1, "total": 1},
            "indicator_categories": ["ESCALATION_GAP"],
            "indicator_emitted_by": {
                "ESCALATION_GAP": "declared",
                "MISSING_ESCALATION_EVIDENCE": "framework.supervision.negative_space_detector.NegativeSpaceDetector"
            }

        },


        "INCIDENT_RESPONSE": {

            "name": "Incident Response",
            "description":
                "Evidence that the CSE responds to and closes incidents, including containment, resolution and lifecycle disposition.",
            "primary_evidence": [
                {
                    "canonical_path": "response_context.resolution_time",
                    "concept": "RESOLUTION_TIME",
                    "role": "recorded resolution of a case"
                }
            ],
            "supporting_evidence": [
                {
                    "canonical_path": "response_context.acknowledgement_time",
                    "concept": null,
                    "role": "acknowledgement timing relative to resolution"
                },
                {
                    "canonical_path": "investigation_context.remediation_identified",
                    "concept": null,
                    "role": "containment or remediation outcome"
                },
                {
                    "canonical_path": "investigation_context.evidence_available",
                    "concept": null,
                    "role": "response evidence retention"
                },
                {
                    "canonical_path": "alert_context.timestamp",
                    "concept": "EVENT_TIMESTAMP",
                    "role": "response reference time"
                }
            ],
            "minimum_evidence": {"primary": 1, "total": 1},
            "indicator_categories": ["FAST_CLOSURE_RISK"],
            "indicator_emitted_by": {
                "FAST_CLOSURE_RISK": "framework.supervision.execution_gap_engine.ExecutionGapEngine"
            }

        },


        "SECURITY_OPERATIONS": {

            "name": "Security Operations",
            "description":
                "Evidence of the operational substrate the SOC runs on: monitored assets, asset importance and monitoring coverage.",
            "primary_evidence": [
                {
                    "canonical_path": "asset_context.asset_id",
                    "concept": "ASSET_IDENTIFIER",
                    "role": "identification of monitored assets"
                }
            ],
            "supporting_evidence": [
                {
                    "canonical_path": "monitoring_context.telemetry_available",
                    "concept": null,
                    "role": "availability of monitoring telemetry"
                },
                {
                    "canonical_path": "monitoring_context.coverage_status",
                    "concept": null,
                    "role": "monitoring coverage state"
                },
                {
                    "canonical_path": "asset_context.criticality",
                    "concept": null,
                    "role": "business importance of monitored assets"
                },
                {
                    "canonical_path": "alert_context.timestamp",
                    "concept": "EVENT_TIMESTAMP",
                    "role": "operational activity over time"
                }
            ],
            "minimum_evidence": {"primary": 1, "total": 3},
            "indicator_categories": ["MONITORING_VISIBILITY_GAP", "ASSET_CRITICALITY_RISK"],
            "indicator_emitted_by": {
                "MONITORING_VISIBILITY_GAP": "declared",
                "ASSET_CRITICALITY_RISK": "declared"
            }

        },


        "GOVERNANCE_OVERSIGHT": {

            "name": "Governance Oversight",
            "description":
                "Evidence of ownership, review and approval over security activity. The presence of alert records is never treated as governance evidence.",
            "primary_evidence": [
                {
                    "canonical_path": "entity_context.entity_name",
                    "concept": "USER_IDENTIFIER",
                    "role": "accountable owner of the activity under review"
                }
            ],
            "supporting_evidence": [
                {
                    "canonical_path": "investigation_context.remediation_identified",
                    "concept": null,
                    "role": "evidence of approved corrective action"
                }
            ],
            "minimum_evidence": {"primary": 1, "total": 1},
            "indicator_categories": [],
            "indicator_emitted_by": {},
            "_note":
                "The canonical schema currently exposes no review, approval, exception or management-review field. Ownership is the only governance signal that exists today, so this capability can rarely reach AVAILABLE. That is reported honestly rather than worked around."

        },


        "OPERATIONAL_DISCIPLINE": {

            "name": "Operational Discipline",
            "description":
                "Evidence of consistent, timely handling practice: closure behaviour, investigation consistency and escalation compliance.",
            "primary_evidence": [
                {
                    "canonical_path": "response_context.resolution_time",
                    "concept": "RESOLUTION_TIME",
                    "role": "closure timing for SLA and handling practice"
                },
                {
                    "canonical_path": "alert_context.severity",
                    "concept": "SECURITY_SEVERITY",
                    "role": "severity against which closure practice is judged"
                }
            ],
            "supporting_evidence": [
                {
                    "canonical_path": "investigation_context.notes",
                    "concept": "INVESTIGATION_EVIDENCE",
                    "role": "consistency of investigation practice"
                },
                {
                    "canonical_path": "alert_context.timestamp",
                    "concept": "EVENT_TIMESTAMP",
                    "role": "reference time for handling intervals"
                },
                {
                    "canonical_path": "response_context.escalation_status",
                    "concept": "ESCALATION_STATUS",
                    "role": "escalation compliance"
                }
            ],
            "minimum_evidence": {"primary": 1, "total": 3},
            "indicator_categories": [
                "INVESTIGATION_QUALITY",
                "FAST_CLOSURE_RISK",
                "ESCALATION_GAP"
            ],
            "indicator_emitted_by": {
                "INVESTIGATION_QUALITY": "framework.supervision.execution_gap_engine.ExecutionGapEngine",
                "FAST_CLOSURE_RISK": "framework.supervision.execution_gap_engine.ExecutionGapEngine",
                "ESCALATION_GAP": "declared"
            }

        },


        "CYBER_RESILIENCE": {

            "name": "Cyber Resilience",
            "description":
                "Evidence that the CSE prevents recurrence and sustains response over time. A single alert is never treated as evidence of resilience.",
            "primary_evidence": [
                {
                    "canonical_path": "response_context.resolution_time",
                    "concept": "RESOLUTION_TIME",
                    "role": "remediation completion for repeated or recurring issues"
                }
            ],
            "supporting_evidence": [
                {
                    "canonical_path": "alert_context.timestamp",
                    "concept": "EVENT_TIMESTAMP",
                    "role": "longitudinal timing needed to observe recurrence"
                },
                {
                    "canonical_path": "investigation_context.remediation_identified",
                    "concept": null,
                    "role": "remediation outcome"
                },
                {
                    "canonical_path": "monitoring_context.coverage_status",
                    "concept": null,
                    "role": "monitoring continuity"
                }
            ],
            "minimum_evidence": {"primary": 1, "total": 3},
            "indicator_categories": [],
            "indicator_emitted_by": {},
            "_note":
                "Recurrence is a property of a time series, and the canonical schema has no concept for incident identity over time. This capability therefore stays at or below INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE for single-scope submissions. Trend analysis is out of scope for this phase and would be the natural future consumer."

        }
    }
}
